---
kind: lore
id: routine
title: The station's routine
---

// The afternoon and night routines play first in every slotStart sequence
// (priority 10); the day's events follow at lower priority.

<beat id="afternoon" on="slotStart" title="One o'clock readings" priority="10" once="false" when="run.slot == 'afternoon'">
  ::bg{location="deck" time="afternoon"}
  ::use{component="reading" hour="One o'clock" instance="use-001"}
  <match on="run.weather">
    <when is="storm">
      @narrator{code="0010"}: Nobody goes anywhere this afternoon. Ines has the kettle on and the charts out.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @narrator{code="0020"}: The afternoon is yours. Ines retreats to the radio room with her charts; the path down to the village glitters.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>

<beat id="night" on="slotStart" title="Seven o'clock, and supper" priority="10" once="false" when="run.slot == 'night' && !(run.day == 7)">
  ::bg{location="kitchen" time="night"}
  ::music{action="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The seven o'clock readings, then supper: lentils, black bread, whatever Pell brought up last.
  @ines{code="0010" emotion="tired" when="run.weather == 'storm'"}: Eat. The wind will still be there after.
  @ines{code="0020" emotion="neutral" when="run.weather != 'storm'"}: Clear tonight. Sol will be insufferable about it.
</beat>

// The day closes. The engine raises dayEnd BEFORE it advances run.day.
<beat id="dayClose" on="dayEnd" title="Lamps out" once="false">
  ::bg{location="bunk" time="night"}
  ::music{action="fadeOut"}
  <match on="clock.weekday">
    <when is="5">
      @narrator{code="0010"}: You lie awake listening to the village band practising, very far below, very badly.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @narrator{code="0020"}: You write the date at the top of tomorrow's page, so the morning has somewhere to start.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>

// Side remark on dayEnd: the day Wren waited at the goat pen for nobody.
<beat id="missedWren" on="dayEnd" title="The path you didn't take" also when="run.day == 3 && !visited('wren.first')">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: From the bunk window you can see the village lights. Someone down there has been expecting a station intern since Monday.
</beat>
